From: junkyard
Subject: [PATCH] radio/samsung/s5300: port to android-mainline

One cumulative patch, kept in two sections: the 6.1 -> 6.18 port this
project first needed for GrapheneOS's 6.18 GKI, then 6.18 -> android-mainline.

== 6.1 -> 6.18 ==
(radio/samsung/s5300: port to Linux 6.18 (lynx))

Port private/google-modules/radio/samsung/s5300 to the GrapheneOS Linux 6.18 GKI for the gs201 lynx build.
Mechanical API migrations, no intended behaviour change:

  - platform_driver.remove returns void (6.11)
  - strlcpy() removed, use strscpy() (6.8)
  - del_timer*() renamed timer_delete*() (6.15)
  - from_timer() renamed timer_container_of() (6.16)
  - hrtimer_init() replaced by hrtimer_setup() (6.15)
  - init_dummy_netdev() removed, use alloc_netdev_dummy() (6.10)
  - per-NAPI gro_flush_timeout (6.13)
  - cpufreq_get_policy() unexported
  - page_frag_cache reworked (encoded_page, page_frag_cache_drain) (6.13)

13 files.

lynx-only (kernel/patches-lynx/): felix builds the 6.1 tree these
drivers were written for.

== 6.18 -> android-mainline ==

Linux 6.18 -> android-mainline (7.3):

  * hrtimer_init() + ->function = f  ->  hrtimer_setup(timer, f, ...).
  * shm_ipc.c: RESERVEDMEM_OF_DECLARE() takes a reserved_mem_ops table;
    node_init gets the fdt node.
---
